\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Juniper MX960 Universal Edge Router (JUNOS)\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000NetComm NP805N wireless ADSL router\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000cpe:/o:blackberry:blackberry_os:10.0\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Microsoft Windows Server 2012 R2\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000cpe:/o:microsoft:windows_server_2012:r2\u0000Apple OS X 10.9 (Mavericks) - 10.11 (El Capitan) or iOS 6 - 10.3 (Darwin 13.0.0 - 16.0.0)\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Dell SonicWALL firewall (SonicOS 5.9)\u0000\u0000\u0000Apple OS X 10.10 (Yosemite) - 10.11 (El Capitan) (Darwin 14.0.0 - 15.6.0)\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Apple OS X 10.9 (Mavericks) (Darwin 13.4.0)\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Microsoft Windows 8.1 or Windows 10\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000cpe:/o:dragonflybsd:dragonfly_bsd:4.7\u0000nsock_iod.c\u0000nsi\u0000basic_string::append\u0000https://nmap.org\u00007.80\u0000Nmap\u0000 ,\u0000CAPACITY <%s> = %d\r\n\u0000mass_rdns: *DR*OPPING <%s>\r\n\u0000void do_possible_writes()\u0000nmap_dns.cc\u0000tpreq != NULL\u0000read_evt_handler\u0000\r\nQUITTING!\r\n\u0000nmaprun\u0000runstats\u0000exit\u0000errormsg\u0000NAXGS\u0000nmap-mac-prefixes\u0000void mac_prefix_init()\u0000MACLookup.cc\u0000*endptr\u0000MACPrefix2Corp\u0000%s called with a NULL prefix\u0000MACCorp2Prefix\u0000%s: vendorstr is NULL\u0000%s: mac_data is NULL\u0000/etc/resolv.conf\u0000nameserver %%%us\u0000o.mass_dns || servs.empty()\u000080,443\u0000nmap.cc\u0000ports.syn_ping_count > 0\u0000%s: %s (%d)\r\n\u0000%s: %s (%d)\u0000/etc/hosts\u0000s %255s\u0000nmap_mass_rdns_core\u0000NmapOps.cc\u0000idle scan against %s\u0000idle_scan\u0000idle_scan.cc\u0000htn.toclock_running == false\u0000]:\u0000initialize_idleproxy\u0000socket troubles in %s\u0000\u0002\u0004\u0005\ufffd\u0000Malformed packet received\u0000%d ports\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000%s %s ( %s )\r\nUsage: nmap [Scan Type(s)] [Options] {target specification}\r\nTARGET SPECIFICATION:\r\n  Can pass hostnames, IP addresses, networks, etc.\r\n  Ex: scanme.nmap.org, microsoft.com/24, 192.168.0.1; 10.0.0-255.1-254\r\n  -iL <inputfilename>: Input from list of hosts/networks\r\n  -iR <num hosts>: Choose random targets\r\n  --exclude <host1[,host2][,host3],...>: Exclude hosts/networks\r\n  --excludefile <exclude_file>: Exclude list from file\r\nHOST DISCOVERY:\r\n  -sL: List Scan - simply list targets to scan\r\n  -sn: Ping Scan - disable port scan\r\n  -Pn: Treat all hosts as online -- skip host discovery\r\n  -PS/PA/PU/PY[portlist]: TCP SYN/ACK, UDP or SCTP discovery to given ports\r\n  -PE/PP/PM: ICMP echo, timestamp, and netmask request discovery probes\r\n  -PO[protocol list]: IP Protocol Ping\r\n  -n/-R: Never do DNS resolution/Always resolve [default: sometimes]\r\n  --dns-servers <serv1[,serv2],...>: Specify custom DNS servers\r\n  --system-dns: Use OS's DNS resolver\r\n  --traceroute: Trace hop path to each host\r\nSCAN TECHNIQUES:\r\n  -sS/sT/sA/sW/sM: TCP SYN/Connect()/ACK/Window/Maimon scans\r\n  -sU: UDP Scan\r\n  -sN/sF/sX: TCP Null, FIN, and Xmas scans\r\n  --scanflags <flags>: Customize TCP scan flags\r\n  -sI <zombie host[:probeport]>: Idle scan\r\n  -sY/sZ: SCTP INIT/COOKIE-ECHO scans\r\n  -sO: IP protocol scan\r\n  -b <FTP relay host>: FTP bounce scan\r\nPORT SPECIFICATION AND SCAN ORDER:\r\n  -p <port ranges>: Only scan specified ports\r\n    Ex: -p22; -p1-65535; -p U:53,111,137,T:21-25,80,139,8080,S:9\r\n  --exclude-ports <port ranges>: Exclude the specified ports from scanning\r\n  -F: Fast mode - Scan fewer ports than the default scan\r\n  -r: Scan ports consecutively - don't randomize\r\n  --top-ports <number>: Scan <number> most common ports\r\n  --port-ratio <ratio>: Scan ports more common than <ratio>\r\nSERVICE/VERSION DETECTION:\r\n  -sV: Probe open ports to determine service/version info\r\n  --version-intensity <level>: Set from 0 (light) to 9 (try all probes)\r\n  --version-light: Limit to most likely probes (intensity 2)\r\n  --version-all: Try every single probe (intensity 9)\r\n  --version-trace: Show detailed version scan activity (for debugging)\r\nSCRIPT SCAN:\r\n  -sC: equivalent to --script=default\r\n  --script=<Lua scripts>: <Lua scripts> is a comma separated list of\r\n           directories, script-files or script-categories\r\n  --script-args=<n1=v1,[n2=v2,...]>: provide arguments to scripts\r\n  --script-args-file=filename: provide NSE script args in a file\r\n  --script-trace: Show all data sent and received\r\n  --script-updatedb: Update the script database.\r\n  --script-help=<Lua scripts>: Show help about scripts.\r\n           <Lua scripts> is a comma-separated list of script-files or\r\n           script-categories.\r\nOS DETECTION:\r\n  -O: Enable OS detection\r\n  --osscan-limit: Limit OS detection to promising targets\r\n  --osscan-guess: Guess OS more aggressively\r\nTIMING AND PERFORMANCE:\r\n  Options which take <time> are in seconds, or append 'ms' (milliseconds),\r\n  's' (seconds), 'm' (minutes), or 'h' (hours) to the value (e.g. 30m).\r\n  -T<0-5>: Set timing template (higher is faster)\r\n  --min-hostgroup/max-hostgroup <size>: Parallel host scan group sizes\r\n  --min-parallelism/max-parallelism <numprobes>: Probe parallelization\r\n  --min-rtt-timeout/max-rtt-timeout/initial-rtt-timeout <time>: Specifies\r\n      probe round trip time.\r\n  --max-retries <tries>: Caps number of port scan probe retransmissions.\r\n  --host-timeout <time>: Give up on target after this long\r\n  --scan-delay/--max-scan-delay <time>: Adjust delay between probes\r\n  --min-rate <number>: Send packets no slower than <number> per second\r\n  --max-rate <number>: Send packets no faster than <number> per second\r\nFIREWALL/IDS EVASION AND SPOOFING:\r\n  -f; --mtu <val>: fragment packets (optionally w/given MTU)\r\n  -D <decoy1,decoy2[,ME],...>: Cloak a scan with decoys\r\n  -S <IP_Address>: Spoof source address\r\n  -e <iface>: Use specified interface\r\n  -g/--source-port <portnum>: Use given port number\r\n  --proxies <url1,[url2],...>: Relay connections through HTTP/SOCKS4 proxies\r\n  --data <hex string>: Append a custom payload to sent packets\r\n  --data-string <string>: Append a custom ASCII string to sent packets\r\n  --data-length <num>: Append random data to sent packets\r\n  --ip-options <options>: Send packets with specified ip options\r\n  --ttl <val>: Set IP time-to-live field\r\n  --spoof-mac <mac address/prefix/vendor name>: Spoof your MAC address\r\n  --badsum: Send packets with a bogus TCP/UDP/SCTP checksum\r\nOUTPUT:\r\n  -oN/-oX/-oS/-oG <file>: Output scan in normal, XML, s|<rIpt kIddi3,\r\n     and Grepable format, respectively, to the given filename.\r\n  -oA <basename>: Output in the three major formats at once\r\n  -v: Increase verbosity level (use -vv or more for greater effect)\r\n  -d: Increase debugging level (use -dd or more for greater effect)\r\n  --reason: Display the reason a port is in a particular state\r\n  --open: Only show open (or possibly open) ports\r\n  --packet-trace: Show all packets sent and received\r\n  --iflist: Print host interfaces and routes (for debugging)\r\n  --append-output: Append to rather than clobber specified output files\r\n  --resume <filename>: Resume an aborted scan\r\n  --stylesheet <path/URL>: XSL stylesheet to transform XML output to HTML\r\n  --webxml: Reference stylesheet from Nmap.Org for more portable XML\r\n  --no-stylesheet: Prevent associating of XSL stylesheet w/XML output\r\nMISC:\r\n  -6: Enable IPv6 scanning\r\n  -A: Enable OS detection, version detection, script scanning, and traceroute\r\n  --datadir <dirname>: Specify custom Nmap data file location\r\n  --send-eth/--send-ip: Send using raw ethernet frames or IP packets\r\n  --privileged: Assume that the user is fully privileged\r\n  --unprivileged: Assume the user lacks raw socket privileges\r\n  -V: Print version number\r\n  -h: Print this help summary page.\r\nEXAMPLES:\r\n  nmap -v -A scanme.nmap.org\r\n  nmap -v -sn 192.168.0.0/16 10.0.0.0/8\r\n  "]
[53.473028, "o", "nmap -v -iR 10000 -Pn -p 80\r\nSEE THE MAN PAGE (https://nmap.org/book/man.html) FOR MORE OPTIONS AND EXAMPLES\r\n\u0000\u0000mass_rdns: %.2fs %d/%d [#: %lu, OK: %d, NX: %d, DR: %d, SF: %d, TR: %d]\r\n\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000mass_rdns: Using DNS server %s\r\n\u0000mass_rdns: TRANSMITTING for <%s> (server <%s>)\r\n\u0000mass_dns: warning: got a %s:%s in %s()\r\n\u0000mass_rdns: NXDOMAIN <id = %d>\r\n\u0000\u0000mass_rdns: SERVFAIL <id = %d>\r\n\u0000\u0000mass_rdns: OK MATCHED <%s> to <%s>\r\n\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000mass_rdns: CNAME found for <%s> to <%s>\r\n\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000mass_rdns: CNAME for <%s> not processed.\r\n\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000mass_rdns: Unable to process the response\r\n\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Output filename begins with '-'. Try '-%s ./%s' if you really want it to be named as such.\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000You are using a deprecated option in a dangerous way. Did you mean: -o%c %s\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Cannot display multiple output types to stdout.\u0000Cannot find nmap-mac-prefixes: Ethernet vendor correlation will not be performed\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Unable to open %s.  Ethernet vendor correlation will not be performed \u0000\u0000Parse error on line #%d of %s. Giving up parsing.\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000MAC prefix %06X is duplicated in %s; ignoring duplicates.\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000mass_dns: warning: Unable to open /etc/resolv.conf. Try using --system-dns or specify valid servers with --dns-servers\u0000\u0000std::__cxx11::list<std::__cxx11::basic_string<char> > get_dns_servers()\u0000Tried to realloc negative amount of memory!!!\u0000\u0000\u0000Realloc Failed! Probably out of space.\u0000\u0000Warning:  You are not root -- using TCP pingscan rather than ICMP\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000void validate_scan_lists(scan_lists&, NmapOps&)\u0000mass_dns: warning: Unable to determine any DNS servers. Reverse DNS is disabled. Try using --system-dns or specify valid servers with --dns-servers\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Unable to create nsock pool in %s()\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000int NmapOps::SourceSockAddr(sockaddr_storage*, size_t*)\u0000Parallel DNS resolution of %d host%s.\u0000\u0000\u0000Performing system-dns for %d domain names that were deferred\r\n\u0000\u0000\u0000System DNS resolution of %u host%s.\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Failed to get target socket address.\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000System DNS resolution of %d host%s.\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000DNS resolution of %d IPs took %.2fs. Mode: Async [#: %lu, OK: %d, NX: %d, DR: %d, SF: %d, TR: %d, CN: %d]\r\n\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000DNS resolution of %d IPs took %.2fs. Mode: System [OK: %d, ??: %d]\r\n\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000idle scan requires a proxy host\u0000%s: You are not allowed to change proxies midstream.  Sorry\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000void idle_scan(Target*, u16*, int, char*, const scan_lists*)\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Skipping Idle Scan against %s -- you can't idle scan your own machine (localhost).\r\n\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000void Target::startTimeOutClock(const timeval*)\u0000\u0000Invalid port number given in IP ID zombie specification: %s\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000void initialize_idleproxy(idle_proxy_info*, char*, Target*, const scan_lists*)\u0000\u0000Could not resolve idle scan zombie host \"%s\": %s\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Unable to find appropriate source address and device interface to use when sending packets to %s\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000%s: Failed to determine dst MAC address for Idle proxy\u0000\u0000Call to pcap_open_live() failed three times. There are several possible reasons for this, depending on your operating system:\r\nLINUX: If you are getting Socket type not supported, try modprobe af_packet or recompile your kernel with PACKET enabled.\r\n *BSD:  If you are getting device not configured, you need to recompile your kernel with Berkeley Packet Filter support.  If you are getting No such file or directory, try creating the device (eg cd /dev; MAKEDEV <device>; or use mknod).\r\n*WINDOWS:  Nmap only supports ethernet interfaces on Windows for most operations because Microsoft disabled raw sockets as of Windows XP SP2.  Depending on the reason for this error, it is possible that the --unprivileged command-line argument will help.\r\nSOLARIS:  If you are trying to scan localhost or the address of an interface and are getting '/dev/lo0: No such file or directory' or 'lo0: No DLPI device found', complain to Sun.  I don't think Solaris can support advanced localhost scans.  You can probably use \"-Pn -sT localhost\" though.\r\n\r\n\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000tcp and src host %s and dst host %s\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Packet capture filter (device %s): %s\r\n\u0000\u0000Error occurred while trying to send IPv6 packet\u0000Received a packet with version field != 4\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Received unexpected response packet from %s during initial IP ID zombie testing\u0000Received a packet with version field != 6\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000IPv6 packet without fragmentation header received - issues with the zombie?\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Idle scan zombie %s (%s) port %hu cannot be used because it has not returned any of our probes -- perhaps it is down or firewalled.\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Idle scan using zombie %s (%s:%hu); Class: %s\r\n\u0000\u0000Idle scan zombie %s (%s) port %hu cannot be used because IP ID sequence class is: %s.  Try another proxy.\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Idle scan initial zombie qualification test: %d probes sent, only %d returned\u0000\u0000\u0000Error occurred while trying to send IPv6 packet \u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Your IP ID Zombie (%s; %s) is behaving strangely -- suddenly cannot obtain IP ID\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Your IP ID Zombie (%s; %s) is behaving strangely -- suddenly cannot obtain valid IP ID distance.\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Even though your Zombie (%s; %s) appears to be vulnerable to IP ID sequence prediction (class: %s), our attempts have failed.  This generally means that either the Zombie uses a separate IP ID base for each host (like Solaris), or because you cannot spoof IP packets (perhaps your ISP has enabled egress filtering to prevent IP spoofing), or maybe the target network recognizes the packet source as bogus and drops them\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000WARNING: IP ID spoofing test sent 4 packets and expected a distance of 5, but instead got %d\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u00000\r\n\ufffd\ufffd\ufffd\r\ufffd\ufffd\ufffd\r\ufffd\ufffd\ufffd\r\ufffd\ufffd\ufffd\r\ufffd\ufffd\ufffd\r\ufffd\ufffd\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000N3DNS12CNAME_RecordE\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000N3DNS10PTR_RecordE\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000N3DNS6RecordE\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000N3DNS8A_RecordE\u0000nsock_iod_set_ipoptions\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\ufffd\u000f\u0000\u0000\ufffd\u000f\u0000\u0000\ufffd\u0013\u0000\u0000\ufffd\ufffd\ufffd\ufffd\ufffd\t\u0000\u0000\ufffd\u000f\u0000\u0000\ufffd\ufffd\ufffd\ufffd\ufffd\ufffd\ufffd\ufffd\ufffd\t\u0000\u0000\ufffd\u000b\u0000\u0000\ufffd\ufffd\ufffd\ufffd\ufffd\ufffd\ufffd\ufffd\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000@\ufffd@ffffff\ufffd?void NmapOps::setSourceSockAddr(sockaddr_storage*, size_t)\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000ss_len > 0 && ss_len <= sizeof(*ss)\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000NmapOutputTableCell* NmapOutputTable::getCellAddy(unsigned int, unsigned int)\u0000\u0000\u0000%s: initial round trip time must be greater than 0\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000%s: maximum round trip time must be greater than 0\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000%s: minimum round trip time must be at least 0\u0000\u0000Minimum host group size may not be set to greater than maximum size (currently %d)\r\n\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Maximum host group size may not be set to less than the minimum size (currently %d)\r\n\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Max host size must be at least 1\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000NmapOutputTable::NmapOutputTable(int, int)\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000NmapOutputTable::~NmapOutputTable()\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000void NmapOutputTable::addItem(unsigned int, unsigned int, bool, const char*, int)\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000NmapOutputTable only supports adding up to 4096 to a cell via %s.\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000bool NmapOutputTable::emptyRow(unsigned int)\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000%s: __pos (which is %zu) > this->size() (which is %zu)\u0000\u0000Assuming %s is a username, and using the default password: %s\r\n\u0000\u0000WARNING: If -S is being used to fake your source address, you may also have to use -e <interface> and -Pn .  If you are using it to specify your real source address, you can ignore this warning.\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000WARNING: Many people use -Pn w/Idlescan to prevent pings from their true IP.  On the other hand, timing info Nmap gains from pings can allow for faster, more reliable scans.\u0000\u0000\u0000WARNING: Your decoys won't be used in the Idlescan portion of your scanning (although all packets sent to the target are spoofed anyway\u0000WARNING: -S will only affect the source address used in a connect() scan if you specify one of your own addresses.  Use -sS or another raw scan if you want to completely spoof your source address, but then you need to know what you're doing to obtain meaningful results.\u0000\u0000Sorry, UDP Ping (-PU) only works if you are root (because we need to read raw responses off the wire)\u0000\u0000\u0000Sorry, SCTP INIT Ping (-PY) only works if you are root (because we need to read raw responses off the wire)\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Sorry, IPProto Ping (-PO) only works if you are root (because we need to read raw responses off the wire)\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Sorry, the IPProtoscan (-sO) must currently be used alone rather than combined with other scan types.\u0000\u0000\u0000-sL and -sn (skip port scan) are not valid with any other scan types\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000ICMP Timestamp and Address Mask pings are only valid for IPv4.\u0000\u0000You requested a scan type which requires %s\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Sorry, but decoys (-D) require %s\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Sorry, but fragscan requires %s\u0000TCP/IP fingerprinting (for OS scan) requires %s\u0000Hint: if your bounce scan target hosts aren't reachable from here, remember to use -Pn so we don't try and ping them prior to the scan\r\n\u0000You specified more than one type of TCP scan.  Please choose only one of -sA, -b, -sT, -sF, -sI, -sM, -sN, -sS, -sW, and -sX\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000WARNING: Decoys are irrelevant to the bounce or connect scans\u0000\u0000\u0000Fragscan only works with TCP, ICMP Timestamp or ICMP Mask (mtu=8) ping types or ACK, FIN, Maimon, NULL, SYN, Window, and XMAS scan types\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Combining bounce scan with OS scan seems silly, but I will let you do whatever you want!\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000WARNING: OS Scan is unreliable without a port scan.  You need to use a scan type along with it, such as -sS, -sT, -sF, etc instead of -sn\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000WARNING: Disabling OS Scan (-O) as it is incompatible with the IPProto Scan (-sO)\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000WARNING: Disabling Service Scan (-sV) as it is incompatible with the IPProto Scan (-sO)\u0000Option --defeat-rst-ratelimit works only with a SYN scan (-sS)\u0000\u0000Option --defeat-icmp-ratelimit works only with a UDP scan (-sU)\u0000WARNING: -g is incompatible with the default connect() scan (-sT).  Use a raw scan such as -sS if you want to set the source port.\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000--min-parallelism=%i must be less than or equal to --max-parallelism=%i\u0000--min-rate=%g must be less than or equal to --max-rate=%g\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Random targets, FTP bounce scan, and fragmentation are not supported with IPv6.\u0000WARNING: IP options are NOT used while OS scanning!\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Bogus --script-timeout argument specified\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Bogus --max-os-tries argument specified, must be between 1 and 50 (inclusive)\u0000\u0000\u0000Bogus --max-rtt-timeout argument specified, must be at least 5ms\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Since April 2010, the default unit for --max-rtt-timeout is seconds, so your time of \"%s\" is %g seconds. Use \"%sms\" for %g milliseconds.\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000WARNING: You specified a round-trip time timeout (%ld ms) that is EXTRAORDINARILY SMALL.  Accuracy may suffer.\u0000\u0000Bogus --min-rtt-timeout argument specified\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Since April 2010, the default unit for --min-rtt-timeout is seconds, so your time of \"%s\" is %g seconds. Use \"%sms\" for %g milliseconds.\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Bogus --initial-rtt-timeout argument specified.  Must be positive\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Since April 2010, the default unit for --initial-rtt-timeout is seconds, so your time of \"%s\" is %g seconds. Use \"%sms\" for %g milliseconds.\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Warning: You specified a highly aggressive --min-hostgroup.\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000--scanflags option must be a number between 0 and 255 (inclusive) or a string like \"URGPSHFIN\".\u0000Argument to --min-parallelism must be at least 1!\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Warning: Your --min-parallelism option is pretty high!  This can hurt reliability.\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Bogus --host-timeout argument specified\u0000Since April 2010, the default unit for --host-timeout is seconds, so your time of \"%s\" is %.1f hours. If this is what you want, use \"%ss\".\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000ttl option must be a number between 0 and 255 (inclusive)\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000version-intensity must be between 0 and 9\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Bogus --scan-delay argument specified.\u0000\u0000Since April 2010, the default unit for --scan-delay is seconds, so your time of \"%s\" is %.1f minutes. Use \"%sms\" for %g milliseconds.\u0000\u0000\u0000Bogus --max-scan-delay argument specified.\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Since April 2010, the default unit for --max-scan-delay is seconds, so your time of \"%s\" is %.1f minutes. If this is what you want, use \"%ss\".\u0000\u0000Unknown or non-available engine: %s\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Invalid proxy chain specification\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Can't use the --data option(s) multiple times, or together.\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000WARNING: Payloads bigger than 1400 bytes may not be sent successfully.\u0000\u0000string length must be between 0 and %d\u0000\u0000data-length must be between 0 and %d\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000https://svn.nmap.org/nmap/docs/nmap.xsl\u0000HTML output is not directly supported, though Nmap includes an XSL for transforming XML output into HTML.  See the man page.\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000!!Greets to Van Hauser, Plasmoid, Skyper and the rest of THC!!\r\n\u0000Only one input filename allowed\u0000Failed to open input file %s for reading\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000ERROR: -iR argument must be the maximum number of random IPs you wish to scan (use 0 for unlimited)\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000ERROR: -sI argument must be less than %d characters\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Data payload MTU must be >0 and multiple of 8\u0000\u0000\u0000--port-ratio should be between [0 and 1)\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Only 1 --exclude-ports option allowed, separate multiple ranges with commas.\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000--top-ports should be an integer 1 or greater\u0000\u0000\u0000Ip options can't be more than 40 bytes long\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Ip options must be multiple of 4 (read length is %i bytes)\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Argument to --min-rate must be a positive floating-point number\u0000Argument to --max-rate must be a positive floating-point number\u0000Bogus --stats-every argument specified\u0000\u0000Cannot use --resume with other options. Usage: nmap --resume <filename>\u0000Unknown long option (%s) given@#!$#$\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Cannot use both -4 and -6 in one scan.\u0000\u0000Your argument to -b is b0rked. Use the normal url style:  user:pass@server:port or just use server and use default anon login\r\n  Use -h for help\u0000WARNING: a source port of zero may not work on all systems.\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000See the output of nmap -h for a summary of options.\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000WARNING: identscan (-I) no longer supported.  Ignoring -I\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Argument to -M must be at least 1!\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Warning: Your max-parallelism (-M) option is extraordinarily high, which can hurt reliability\u0000\u0000\u0000First-generation OS detection (-O1) is no longer supported. Use -O instead.\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000The -PR option is deprecated. ARP scan is always done when possible.\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Only one -PS option is allowed. Combine port ranges with commas.\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000void parse_options(int, char**)\u0000Only one -PB, -PA, or -PT option is allowed. Combine port ranges with commas.\u0000\u0000\u0000Only one -PU option is allowed. Combine port ranges with commas.\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Only one -PY option is allowed. Combine port ranges with commas.\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Only one -PO option is allowed. Combine protocol ranges with commas.\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Illegal Argument to -P, use -Pn, -PE, -PS, -PA, -PP, -PM, -PU, -PY, or -PO\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Only 1 -p option allowed, separate multiple ranges with commas.\u0000You can only use the source option once!  Use -D <decoy1> -D <decoy2> etc. for decoys\r\n\u0000\u0000An option is required for -s, most common are -sT (tcp scan), -sS (SYN scan), -sF (FIN scan), -sU (UDP scan) and -sn (Ping scan)\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000No scan type 'B', did you mean bounce scan (-b)?\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000WARNING: -sR is now an alias for -sV and activates version detection as well as RPC scan.\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Unknown timing mode (-T argument).  Use either \"Paranoid\", \"Sneaky\", \"Polite\", \"Normal\", \"Aggressive\", \"Insane\" or a number from 0 (Paranoid) to 5 (Insane)\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Could not assign %s to stdout for writing\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u000046Ab:D:d::e:Ffg:hIi:M:m:nO::o:P::p:qRrS:s::T:Vv::\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000without the necessary privileges\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Failed to resolve/decode supposed %s source address \"%s\": %s\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Warning: --min-parallelism and --max-parallelism are ignored with --scan-delay.\u0000Binary ip options to be send:\r\n%s\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Parsed ip options to be send:\r\n%s\r\n\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Unable to properly format time\u0000\u0000Happy %d%s Birthday to Nmap, may it live to be %d!\r\n\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Nmap wishes you a merry Christmas! Specify -sX for Xmas Scan (https://nmap.org/book/man-port-scanning-techniques.html).\r\n\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Traceroute has to be run as root\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Traceroute does not support idle scan\u0000\u0000\u0000You cannot use -F (fast scan) or -p (explicit port selection) when not doing a port scan\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000You cannot use -F (fast scan) with -p (explicit port selection) but see --top-ports and --port-ratio to fast scan a range of ports\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Bogus --spoof-mac value encountered (%s) -- only up to 6 bytes permitted\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Could not parse as a prefix nor find as a vendor substring the given --spoof-mac argument: %s.  If you are giving hex digits, there must be an even number of them.\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Spoofing MAC address %02X:%02X:%02X:%02X:%02X:%02X (%s)\r\n\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000WARNING: Running Nmap setuid, as you are doing, is a major security risk.\r\n\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000WARNING: Running Nmap setgid, as you are doing, is a major security risk.\r\n\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000WARNING: a TCP scan type was requested, but no tcp ports were specified.  Skipping this scan type.\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000WARNING: a SCTP scan type was requested, but no sctp ports were specified.  Skipping this scan type.\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000WARNING: UDP scan was requested, but no udp ports were specified.  Skipping this scan type.\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000WARNING: protocol scan was requested, but no protocols were specified to be scanned.  Skipping this scan type.\u0000\u0000WARNING: a TCP ping scan was requested, but after excluding requested TCP ports, none remain. Skipping this scan t"]
[53.474468, "o", "ype.\u0000\u0000WARNING: a UDP ping scan was requested, but after excluding requested UDP ports, none remain. Skipping this scan type.\u0000\u0000WARNING: a SCTP ping scan was requested, but after excluding requested SCTP ports, none remain. Skipping this scan type.\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000WARNING: a IP Protocol ping scan was requested, but after excluding requested protocols, none remain. Skipping this scan type.\u0000\u0000Could not figure out what device to send the packet out on with the source address you gave me!  If you are trying to sp00f your scan, this is normal, just give the -e eth0 or -e ppp0 or whatever.  Otherwise you can still use -e, but I find it kind of fishy.\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000I cannot figure out what source address to use for device %s, does it even exist?\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Failed to open exclude file %s for reading\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Can only use 'ME' as a decoy once.\r\n\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Random decoys can only be used with IPv4\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000You are only allowed %d decoys (if you need more redefine MAX_DECOYS in nmap.h)\u0000Failed to resolve decoy host \"%s\": %s\u0000\u0000\u0000You have specified some options that require raw socket access.\r\nThese options will not be honored %s.\u0000\u0000\u0000Could not mmap() %s file. Make sure you have enough rights and the file really exists.\u0000\u0000Output file %s is too short -- no use resuming\u0000\u0000Unable to parse supposed log file %s.  Are you sure this is an Nmap output file?\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Unable to parse supposed log file %s: unclosed quote.\u0000\u0000\u0000Unable to parse supposed log file %s.  Sorry\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Unable to parse supposed log file %s.  Perhaps the Nmap execution had not finished at least one host?  In that case there is no use \"resuming\"\u0000\u0000WARNING: You are attempting to resume a scan which used --randomize-hosts.  Some hosts in the last randomized batch may be missed and others may be repeated once\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Unable to parse ip (%s) in supposed log file %s.  Sorry\u0000Warning: You asked for --resume but it doesn't look like any hosts in the log file were successfully scanned.  Starting from the beginning.\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000gather_logfile_resumption_state\u0000int nmap_fetchfile_sub(char*, int, const char*)\u0000Warning: File %s exists, but Nmap is using %s for security and consistency reasons.  set NMAPDIR=. to give priority to files in your local directory (may affect the other data files too).\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Attempting connection to ftp://%s:%s@%s:%i\r\n\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Your FTP bounce proxy server won't talk to us!\u0000\u0000recv problem from FTP bounce server\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Your FTP bounce server doesn't like the username \"%s\"\u0000\u0000\u0000Login credentials accepted by FTP server!\r\n\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Timeout from bounce server ...\u0000\u0000Your FTP bounce server refused login combo (%s/%s)\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Interactive keyboard commands:\r\n?               Display this information\r\nv/V             Increase/decrease verbosity\r\nd/D             Increase/decrease debugging\r\np/P             Enable/disable packet tracing\r\nanything else   Print status\r\nMore help: https://nmap.org/book/man-runtime-interaction.html\r\n\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Our FTP proxy server hung up on us!  retrying\r\n\u0000\u0000Our socket descriptor is dead and we are out of retries. Giving up.\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000result of port query on port %i: %s\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Your FTP bounce server sucks, it won't let us feed bogus ports!\u0000Your FTP bounce server doesn't allow privileged ports, skipping them.\u0000\u0000\u0000And you didn't want to scan any unprivileged ports.  Giving up.\u0000FTP command misalignment detected ... correcting.\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Changed my mind about port %i\r\n\u0000\u0000Warning: %s may not work correctly on Windows Subsystem for Linux.\r\nFor best performance and accuracy, use the native Windows build from %s/download.html#windows.\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Failed to resolve FTP bounce proxy hostname/IP: %s\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Resolved FTP bounce attack proxy to %s (%s).\r\n\u0000\u0000\u0000 %s %s scan initiated %s as: %s \u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000%s %s scan initiated %s as: %s\u0000\u0000WARNING: Your specified max_parallel_sockets of %d, but your system says it might only give us %d.  Trying anyway\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000The max # of sockets we are using is: %d\r\n\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000--------------- Timing report ---------------\r\n\u0000\u0000  rtt-timeouts: init %d, min %d, max %d\r\n\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000  max-scan-delay: TCP %d, UDP %d, SCTP %d\r\n\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000  parallelism: min %d, max %d\r\n\u0000\u0000  max-retries: %d, host-timeout: %ld\r\n\u0000\u0000\u0000---------------------------------------------\r\n\u0000\u0000Cannot get hostname!  Try using -S <my_IP_address> or -e <interface to scan through>\r\n\u0000\u0000\u0000WARNING: We could not determine for sure which interface to use, so we are guessing %s .  If this is wrong, use -S <my_IP_address>.\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Do not have appropriate device name for target\u0000\u0000void returnhost(HostGroupState*)\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Skipping host %s due to host timeout\r\n\u0000\u0000\u0000Host: %s (%s)\tStatus: Timeout\r\n\u0000NmapOutputTable.h\u0000col < numColumns\u0000setMaxRetransmissions\u0000%s: must be positive\u0000setInitialRttTimeout\u0000setMaxRttTimeout\u0000setMinRttTimeout\u0000setMaxOSTries\u0000%s: value must be at least 1\u0000vector::reserve\u0000NmapOutp