ever asked to be done\r\n\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000PortList::isTCPwrapped(%d) requested but port has not been service scanned yet\r\n\u0000PortList::isTCPwrapped(%d) requested but service has no name\r\n\u0000\u0000\u0000void print_state_summary(PortList*, short unsigned int)\u0000%s pingprobe type %s is inappropriate for this scan type; resetting.\r\n\u0000\u0000\u0000Found %s in incomplete hosts list.\r\n\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Found %s in completed hosts list.\r\n\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000%s: failed to allocate temporary memory\u0000Final times for host: srtt: %d rttvar: %d  to: %d\r\n\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000 Note -- the actual IP also responded.\u0000\u0000 Still scanning it due to ping response from its own IP\u0000Host: %s (%s)\tStatus: Smurf (%d responses)\r\n\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Host seems to be a subnet broadcast address (returned %d extra pings).%s\r\n\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Host seems to be a subnet broadcast address (returned %d extra pings). %s.\r\n\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000char* num_to_string_sigdigits(double, int)\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000n > 0 && n < (int) sizeof(buf)\u0000\u0000Expected \"udp\" at line %lu of %s.\r\n\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Expected a port list at line %lu of %s.\r\n\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Can't parse port list \"%s\" at line %lu of %s.\r\n\u0000\u0000Cannot find %s. UDP payloads are disabled.\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000void PortList::setPortState(u16, u8, int)\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000%s: attempt to add port number %d with illegal state %d\r\n\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000protocol!=IPPROTO_IP || portno<256\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Deleting port %hu/%s, which we thought was %s\r\n\u0000\u0000Unable to find nmap-protocols!  Resorting to /etc/protocols\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Unable to open %s for reading protocol information\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000