[53.476773, "o", "escan_countopen correctly found %d open ports (out of %d, starting with %hu)\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Adjusting timing because my first scan of %d ports, starting with %hu found %d open, while second scan yielded %d\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000icmp6 and src host %s and dst host %s\u0000\u0000\u0000Error occurred while trying to send ICMPv6 Echo Request to the idle host\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Idle scan zombie %s (%s) port %hu cannot be used because it has not returned any of our ICMPv6 Echo Requests -- perhaps it is down or firewalled.\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Error occurred while trying to send spoofed ICMPv6 Echo Request to the idle host\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Error occurred while trying to send ICMPv6 PTB to the idle host\u0000COOKIE-ECHO\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000(unknown)\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000333333\ufffd?\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\ufffd\ufffd\u001eA\ufffd\ufffd\ufffd\ufffd\ufffd\ufffd\ufffd?\ufffd\ufffd\ufffd\ufffd\ufffd\ufffd\ufffd?basic_string::_M_construct null not valid\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000nse->sslinfo.ssl_desire == SSL_ERROR_WANT_READ || nse->sslinfo.ssl_desire == SSL_ERROR_WANT_WRITE\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Unknown event type (%d) for IOD #%lu\r\n\u0000\u0000\u0000Bogus seq number request to %s -- type is %s\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000void end_svcprobe(nsock_pool, serviceprobestate, ServiceGroup*, ServiceNFO*, nsock_iod)\u0000member != SG->services_remaining.end()\u0000\u0000Service scan: Not probing some ports due to low intensity\r\n\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000Starting probes against new service: %s:%hu (%s)\r\n\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000int launchSomeServiceProbes(nsock_pool, ServiceGroup*)\u0000\u0000Service scan sending probe %s to %s:%hu (%s)\r\n\u0000\u0000\u0000int send_probe_text(nsock_pool, nsock_iod, ServiceNFO*, ServiceProbe*)\u0000Unknown event type %d\u0000tcpseq\u000